  "architecturalPlan": {
    "scaleRationale": "This is a compact but generous single-level family residence: three connected envelopes reserve capacity for four bedrooms, bathrooms, circulation, storage and living without using property value as an area formula. The approximately 220 m² enclosed footprint is a design choice sized for a contemporary family house, while the pool, covered dining terrace and private garden reserve remain distinct outdoor rooms.",
    "arrivalAndCirculation": "A limestone approach plate leads from the +Z arrival side to a recessed, operable front door at the 0.15 m walking datum; all occupied accommodation is on this same accessible ground datum. Public living occupies the central volume, quieter bedroom capacity occupies the two lateral wings, and the rear garden door connects the living zone directly to the covered terrace and pool deck; no upper level or service fit-out is constructed.",
    "volumeHierarchy": "The 12 x 8 m central living volume is the primary shared room, with 6 x 12 m and 6 x 10 m lower-profile bedroom wings extending to either side. All slabs top out at 0.15 m, enclosure heads are 3.35 m, and the coordinated 0.16 m roof plates establish a calm 3.51 m overall parapet datum; the dining canopy is subordinate at 3.30 m.",
    "relationshipsAndViews": "Arrival is organized on the +Z side, while the house opens toward the -Z terrace, rectangular pool and intentionally unbuilt private-garden reserve beyond. A real rear garden door gives the living room a dry route to the dining terrace, which abuts the pool's near deck without crossing water; side-wing glazing keeps bedroom outlooks more controlled.",
    "roofFacadeAndMaterials": "Flat limestone roof plates, ivory walls, bronze framed openings and timber canopy members create a restrained contemporary identity with deep shade at the dining terrace. Living-facing glazing is concentrated at the terrace and pool side, while the bedroom wings use smaller separated side windows and solid end walls for privacy; all elevations are modelled with a coordinated roof edge, though interior subdivisions remain deferred.",
